{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
  "rate": "-15%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "90",
      "revision": "m09p90-sap-official-primers-andrew-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "4c62f129713a5e0fa64ba8e6e386df7403831f98dbded2f909e6d2bfff5af0a4",
        "2": "4c62f129713a5e0fa64ba8e6e386df7403831f98dbded2f909e6d2bfff5af0a4",
        "3": "4c62f129713a5e0fa64ba8e6e386df7403831f98dbded2f909e6d2bfff5af0a4",
        "4": "4c62f129713a5e0fa64ba8e6e386df7403831f98dbded2f909e6d2bfff5af0a4"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "companion-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Amazon Cloud Front delivers content from locations close to your users. When it needs to fetch content, it contacts an origin. An origin is simply where the content comes from.",
          "text_sha256": "096ee25e40279dfd22f52f5b73ec58af645e2320ede587598b44bb68718d3c4b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7c9e73438479333e5e2949f6717bf166c9fcc26e8b9e4541d64778262ba0c49a",
          "asset_sha256": "4c62f129713a5e0fa64ba8e6e386df7403831f98dbded2f909e6d2bfff5af0a4"
        },
        {
          "id": "companion-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The viewer connects over H T T P S, which encrypts that connection. If you enable A W S waf, it can filter web requests. A W S Shield Standard provides baseline protection against distributed denial of service attacks.",
          "text_sha256": "078c013255a9425cf9057a06f98f8cc3cdbb8a6449c955a9bc60bf0221cf0cfe",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3d8a4e0a135ffcb0b6d5f4f9cfe228a47794d5afaf0e534e068b60cd5a616bda",
          "asset_sha256": "4c62f129713a5e0fa64ba8e6e386df7403831f98dbded2f909e6d2bfff5af0a4"
        },
        {
          "id": "companion-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "For product photos or downloads, use Amazon S three as the origin. Keep the bucket private and use Origin Access Control with a bucket policy that lets your Cloud Front distribution read the files.",
          "text_sha256": "02dc27485e98f3a9cae9c3fdf3f575a30a0db25f9bab4a314cecaef41b1cd34f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b739957b6f00dc1560f44e790e4a743bb6dbfc9c41b0cf275934fc2f183f244f",
          "asset_sha256": "4c62f129713a5e0fa64ba8e6e386df7403831f98dbded2f909e6d2bfff5af0a4"
        },
        {
          "id": "companion-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "If a running web application needs to generate the response, an Application Load Balancer can be the origin. It forwards the request to the app. That is the difference: stored files versus a running application.",
          "text_sha256": "4c31ed3bc6d6501abe4eed32464f18028c31ae05afab7de993e93dc9257bbd9a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4c31ed3bc6d6501abe4eed32464f18028c31ae05afab7de993e93dc9257bbd9a",
          "asset_sha256": "4c62f129713a5e0fa64ba8e6e386df7403831f98dbded2f909e6d2bfff5af0a4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "90",
      "revision": "m11p90-sap-official-primers-andrew-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "d098bbe7e76f10d97f771bd7406b12fa55051bb421e34226069ca85aa56fe3ed",
        "2": "d098bbe7e76f10d97f771bd7406b12fa55051bb421e34226069ca85aa56fe3ed",
        "3": "d098bbe7e76f10d97f771bd7406b12fa55051bb421e34226069ca85aa56fe3ed",
        "4": "d098bbe7e76f10d97f771bd7406b12fa55051bb421e34226069ca85aa56fe3ed"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "rds-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Amazon R D S is a managed service for running a relational database in A W S. Relational databases store records in tables. An app uses S Q L to find or change those records.",
          "text_sha256": "7c6356395b7f66ac41fd545591fdf90d77444116ea612527fe17d000838503ef",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "49b32b647f4c0953d3758d8ec9fc3272dbca53f5c0ae1bdfeab4efbbd39aaf57",
          "asset_sha256": "d098bbe7e76f10d97f771bd7406b12fa55051bb421e34226069ca85aa56fe3ed"
        },
        {
          "id": "rds-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Take this bookstore. When someone looks up order one thousand forty-two, the app sends a S Q L query to the orders table. The row for that order shows Mia and a total of twenty-four dollars.",
          "text_sha256": "01c854280f650695552c4793040b9813164e2727badd0c8d313797d9ad279d5b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "881b9ff097d65755a1eff634ef1d65d376a3eaf114f5e9be61208b5088b50363",
          "asset_sha256": "d098bbe7e76f10d97f771bd7406b12fa55051bb421e34226069ca85aa56fe3ed"
        },
        {
          "id": "rds-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "What does managed mean here? A W S handles tasks such as automated backups and database maintenance. You still decide how the tables are organized, write the queries, and control who can access the data.",
          "text_sha256": "b7ea488e32cde21fe5af21ca199a4337088bb7e7480f286e3bc1e7bd334f83bd",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e9560f61cbb9c672c10382b18bdd844cc699d7f11b7b4d6b67643f8fbfb4a330",
          "asset_sha256": "d098bbe7e76f10d97f771bd7406b12fa55051bb421e34226069ca85aa56fe3ed"
        },
        {
          "id": "rds-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Choose an engine the app supports, such as Postgres Q L, My S Q L, or S Q L Server. The key idea is that R D S manages the database infrastructure, while your application still works with a familiar relational database.",
          "text_sha256": "3717c483488249e8cbe06a1f59badc5a8ab335911d6fb7eb810bcca2d498ae3e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0c2199c7356337bdbb03218a9ce9b0059e3eefed73eb417166194cd786092fc0",
          "asset_sha256": "d098bbe7e76f10d97f771bd7406b12fa55051bb421e34226069ca85aa56fe3ed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "91",
      "revision": "m11p91-sap-official-primers-andrew-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "0a54e66c97d6c8d6b97224e7c1a71e24f1f4a6d0129dc5c43d616c783b7c2991",
        "2": "0a54e66c97d6c8d6b97224e7c1a71e24f1f4a6d0129dc5c43d616c783b7c2991",
        "3": "0a54e66c97d6c8d6b97224e7c1a71e24f1f4a6d0129dc5c43d616c783b7c2991",
        "4": "0a54e66c97d6c8d6b97224e7c1a71e24f1f4a6d0129dc5c43d616c783b7c2991"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "aurora-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Amazon Aurora is a managed relational database you run through Amazon R D S. It works with My S Q L or Postgres Q L, so the app can use familiar S Q L to work with its data.",
          "text_sha256": "29040a6c6660f6ae4229cbf44b97c94e380c914f39da3bca1c756e1a784bcdd5",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "eb72cb4e1b8dc92f0a817d700a069ff8264cfcbfff9408338cd44bc40fd6ff38",
          "asset_sha256": "0a54e66c97d6c8d6b97224e7c1a71e24f1f4a6d0129dc5c43d616c783b7c2991"
        },
        {
          "id": "aurora-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Follow the checkout app. When someone places an order, the update goes to the writer. A reporting app, which mostly reads data, can use an optional reader instead.",
          "text_sha256": "7df5bcf7af9eff1e52238e8e0c2265143c19320c83ef55ea8f9fa6922c08b8c9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7df5bcf7af9eff1e52238e8e0c2265143c19320c83ef55ea8f9fa6922c08b8c9",
          "asset_sha256": "0a54e66c97d6c8d6b97224e7c1a71e24f1f4a6d0129dc5c43d616c783b7c2991"
        },
        {
          "id": "aurora-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Both instances use the same cluster storage. Aurora keeps copies across three Availability Zones. Adding a reader does not mean creating a separate copy of the entire database for that reader.",
          "text_sha256": "002ec2a301d4492cfada49ee1363a4372f63385d4438dea4b74b9e67efa9873b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "002ec2a301d4492cfada49ee1363a4372f63385d4438dea4b74b9e67efa9873b",
          "asset_sha256": "0a54e66c97d6c8d6b97224e7c1a71e24f1f4a6d0129dc5c43d616c783b7c2991"
        },
        {
          "id": "aurora-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "The useful distinction is between storage and compute. Add a reader when you need more capacity for reads. In the cluster shown here, the writer still handles changes.",
          "text_sha256": "cd8fe82cca7f16e07d5d05f95433c922483c3c83e85bed537d15f423f4c73f68",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "cd8fe82cca7f16e07d5d05f95433c922483c3c83e85bed537d15f423f4c73f68",
          "asset_sha256": "0a54e66c97d6c8d6b97224e7c1a71e24f1f4a6d0129dc5c43d616c783b7c2991"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "92",
      "revision": "m11p92-sap-official-primers-andrew-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "fa4e417a874b3d4fc35672b55adad769079fabbb7d45895514ed6682eab3d20b",
        "2": "fa4e417a874b3d4fc35672b55adad769079fabbb7d45895514ed6682eab3d20b",
        "3": "fa4e417a874b3d4fc35672b55adad769079fabbb7d45895514ed6682eab3d20b",
        "4": "fa4e417a874b3d4fc35672b55adad769079fabbb7d45895514ed6682eab3d20b"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "dynamodb-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Amazon Dynamo D B is a managed no S Q L database for apps that find data by key. Here the app needs to show one player's results, without asking a relational database to join multiple tables.",
          "text_sha256": "9b6fcc01e378a98c6a50aa986cb098bee0f6297931e52b3b86a448e9fb55b190",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0c9ddf57ef4859dca138b4644eff0be683082568806d6fcc6aff67204e77f6e6",
          "asset_sha256": "fa4e417a874b3d4fc35672b55adad769079fabbb7d45895514ed6682eab3d20b"
        },
        {
          "id": "dynamodb-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The game asks for Alex. Player ID is the partition key, so the query can ask for the items that share that value. These two highlighted rows are the matches.",
          "text_sha256": "ad8129a3236dd0fe329af2a95eda14cd067284edadd55b2553c7c40622ac3578",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ad8129a3236dd0fe329af2a95eda14cd067284edadd55b2553c7c40622ac3578",
          "asset_sha256": "fa4e417a874b3d4fc35672b55adad769079fabbb7d45895514ed6682eab3d20b"
        },
        {
          "id": "dynamodb-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Race ID is the sort key. It distinguishes Alex's results for different races. The app gets a score of nine hundred for race seven and seven hundred forty for race eight. Maya's row is not included.",
          "text_sha256": "215fc771de560c4a0357c63d49b79a3e8ebdaa808eda5801aad106bf285a1eec",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "215fc771de560c4a0357c63d49b79a3e8ebdaa808eda5801aad106bf285a1eec",
          "asset_sha256": "fa4e417a874b3d4fc35672b55adad769079fabbb7d45895514ed6682eab3d20b"
        },
        {
          "id": "dynamodb-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Start with what the app needs to look up. Then choose keys that let it answer that question directly. Dynamo D B does not use relational joins.",
          "text_sha256": "54773107a9e85252be4ef73b893ba7686394a4047a30d4967b6ff4f13da8d991",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8e724701c1c976c4003597c0576e158a3d7f2b3f82b1fe5f708ac30a385ec749",
          "asset_sha256": "fa4e417a874b3d4fc35672b55adad769079fabbb7d45895514ed6682eab3d20b"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "93",
      "revision": "m11p93-sap-official-primers-andrew-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "9df106fdd68c4dbfc013ba1c1ec66bc37bac589dd9aaa117e2edcf4044df821e",
        "2": "9df106fdd68c4dbfc013ba1c1ec66bc37bac589dd9aaa117e2edcf4044df821e",
        "3": "9df106fdd68c4dbfc013ba1c1ec66bc37bac589dd9aaa117e2edcf4044df821e",
        "4": "9df106fdd68c4dbfc013ba1c1ec66bc37bac589dd9aaa117e2edcf4044df821e"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "kinesis-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Amazon Kinesis Data Streams collects events as they happen. Instead of waiting for a daily export, an application can read a continuous stream of events, like orders coming into an online store.",
          "text_sha256": "27e4d6e72350e27e357d19fcebd26c2f0b5bf70f0c9858d2f044ee00b38e2b92",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "27e4d6e72350e27e357d19fcebd26c2f0b5bf70f0c9858d2f044ee00b38e2b92",
          "asset_sha256": "9df106fdd68c4dbfc013ba1c1ec66bc37bac589dd9aaa117e2edcf4044df821e"
        },
        {
          "id": "kinesis-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The store publishes each event as a record. A shard is one lane in the stream. Here, order forty-two was placed and then paid in one lane. Order seventeen is in a different lane.",
          "text_sha256": "283fe5f38a1e6c42907c9942285c2a05bef61552368f75b4d56e673914ee2531",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "283fe5f38a1e6c42907c9942285c2a05bef61552368f75b4d56e673914ee2531",
          "asset_sha256": "9df106fdd68c4dbfc013ba1c1ec66bc37bac589dd9aaa117e2edcf4044df821e"
        },
        {
          "id": "kinesis-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Two applications can read the stream for different reasons. A sales dashboard counts orders while a fraud application looks for suspicious activity. Each consumer reads and processes the records it needs.",
          "text_sha256": "0dabc1200e18702970c2b2ffe302a5e0560b8ca8ee9a03280507c29b6d81bf63",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0dabc1200e18702970c2b2ffe302a5e0560b8ca8ee9a03280507c29b6d81bf63",
          "asset_sha256": "9df106fdd68c4dbfc013ba1c1ec66bc37bac589dd9aaa117e2edcf4044df821e"
        },
        {
          "id": "kinesis-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "A reader can follow the records in order within a shard. Do not assume a single order across the whole stream. That matters when one event must be handled before the next.",
          "text_sha256": "75e82273fc5d75a1e3902fbdd18da99d5b9938fbf7782e26337275eed0440b09",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "75e82273fc5d75a1e3902fbdd18da99d5b9938fbf7782e26337275eed0440b09",
          "asset_sha256": "9df106fdd68c4dbfc013ba1c1ec66bc37bac589dd9aaa117e2edcf4044df821e"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "94",
      "revision": "m11p94-sap-official-primers-andrew-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "fba717cd055c2ec8d5cb13cf9dfd81e8c2a5e23e12f59c62b9110ae0fe66368a",
        "2": "fba717cd055c2ec8d5cb13cf9dfd81e8c2a5e23e12f59c62b9110ae0fe66368a",
        "3": "fba717cd055c2ec8d5cb13cf9dfd81e8c2a5e23e12f59c62b9110ae0fe66368a",
        "4": "fba717cd055c2ec8d5cb13cf9dfd81e8c2a5e23e12f59c62b9110ae0fe66368a"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "elasticache-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Amazon Elasti Cache is a managed in-memory cache. It keeps copies of frequently used data in memory, so an app does not have to make the same database request every time.",
          "text_sha256": "0a7c88464d091b07878f2e9c4aa3de4e2140f13c640f2d9d08186df9f31c9bbc",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "36f05f2729b10e0e2fdc052fdee6ef6194bda870addadc4e4bbd66210efbbc3d",
          "asset_sha256": "fba717cd055c2ec8d5cb13cf9dfd81e8c2a5e23e12f59c62b9110ae0fe66368a"
        },
        {
          "id": "elasticache-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Imagine a shopper opens product forty-two. The app checks the cache first. If the product is already there, the app uses the cached copy and skips the database. That's a cache hit.",
          "text_sha256": "971d5a8874e2eb89ce87fe87ff18f55ed9603cd9fe4ad4f54aad7257c2973060",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "971d5a8874e2eb89ce87fe87ff18f55ed9603cd9fe4ad4f54aad7257c2973060",
          "asset_sha256": "fba717cd055c2ec8d5cb13cf9dfd81e8c2a5e23e12f59c62b9110ae0fe66368a"
        },
        {
          "id": "elasticache-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "If the product is missing, the app reads it from the database and puts a copy in the cache. The next request can use that copy. That's a cache miss followed by a fill.",
          "text_sha256": "bb047813c480d4e507d2e92dc65a090b26f66677cd2ab1de22cf1645d1a6dd0a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "bb047813c480d4e507d2e92dc65a090b26f66677cd2ab1de22cf1645d1a6dd0a",
          "asset_sha256": "fba717cd055c2ec8d5cb13cf9dfd81e8c2a5e23e12f59c62b9110ae0fe66368a"
        },
        {
          "id": "elasticache-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "In this pattern, the application decides what to do when a request misses, and how long a copy should stay in the cache. The database is still the source of truth.",
          "text_sha256": "73e762b856da4a90abd85d79c2549b87313052ca72d6895471d6bfb5b56f9656",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "73e762b856da4a90abd85d79c2549b87313052ca72d6895471d6bfb5b56f9656",
          "asset_sha256": "fba717cd055c2ec8d5cb13cf9dfd81e8c2a5e23e12f59c62b9110ae0fe66368a"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
